# Exchange Patterns

## Abstract Base Class

All exchange clients MUST inherit from `ExchangeBase` in `backend/exchange/base.py` and implement every abstract method. This ensures paper and live trading are fully interchangeable.

## Required Interface

```python
class ExchangeBase(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    async def get_balance(self) -> dict[str, float]: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def get_ticker(self, symbol: str) -> Ticker: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def get_ohlcv(self, symbol: str, timeframe: str, limit: int) -> pd.DataFrame: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def create_order(self, symbol: str, side: str, order_type: str, amount: float, price: float | None = None) -> Order: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def cancel_order(self, order_id: str, symbol: str) -> None: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def get_open_orders(self, symbol: str | None = None) -> list[Order]: ...

    @abstractmethod
    async def close(self) -> None: ...
```

## Rules

- `PaperExchange` must simulate fills using real market prices (from Binance WebSocket data)
- `BinanceClient` wraps CCXT async — handle rate limits with exponential backoff
- Never expose raw CCXT objects outside the exchange module — always return project-defined dataclasses (Ticker, Order, etc.)
- Factory function `create_exchange(config)` returns the correct client based on `config.mode`
